.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH self-check 1  "self-check " 
.SH NAME
self\-check \- Verify this binary against the published release checksums (Peak C10). Always prints the binary\*(Aqs own SHA\-256; with \-\-archive it verifies a downloaded release archive against the published SHA256SUMS (fetched online, or read from \-\-sums offline)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBself\-check\fR [\fB\-\-archive\fR] [\fB\-\-sums\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Verify this binary against the published release checksums (Peak C10). Always prints the binary\*(Aqs own SHA\-256; with \-\-archive it verifies a downloaded release archive against the published SHA256SUMS (fetched online, or read from \-\-sums offline)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-archive\fR \fI<ARCHIVE>\fR
A downloaded release archive to verify
.TP
\fB\-\-sums\fR \fI<SUMS>\fR
A local SHA256SUMS file to verify against (instead of fetching the published one)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  fg self\-check
  fg self\-check \-\-archive forgehub\-0.1.6\-x86_64\-unknown\-linux\-gnu.tar.gz
  fg self\-check \-\-archive release.tar.gz \-\-sums SHA256SUMS
